ds/nyt_des">Youth</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Teens</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Consumer protection</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Product liability</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Children</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/08/06/multimedia/06biz-meta-new-mexico-clph/06biz-meta-new-mexico-clph-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg" medium="image"><media:credit>Peter Dasilva/Reuters</media:credit><media:description>A New Mexico judge ordered Meta to pay $567 million and make changes to the way young people can use its platform</media:description></media:content></item></channel></rss>